    "title": "Portland and Deering High Schools to Celebrate 113th Turkey Day Football Game on Thanksgiving Morning - NewsBreak",
    "text": "1 hours ago The annual Turkey Day football game between Portland High School and Deering High School will mark its 113th anniversary in 2025. The game started in 1911 and has only been canceled twice: in 1920 because of an ice storm and in 2020 due to the pandemic.\nSince 1967, the game has been held as an exhibition, not as part of the regular season. This year, the game will be at Memorial Field at Deering High School. Kickoff is set for 10 a.m. on Thanksgiving morning.\nVisit here for more details This post includes content assisted by AI tools. Please refer to the source for verification and additional information. Learn more.",
